  "question": {
    "text": "A bacterial infection in an internal wound grows as <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#39;</mi></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> , where the time <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></math> is in hours. A dose of antibiotic, taken orally, needs 1 hour to reach the wound. Once it reaches there, the bacterial population goes down as <math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> . What will be the plot of <math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> vs <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></math> after <math><mn>1</mn></math> hour?"
  },
